86456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287570 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287570 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287570 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186284963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287570 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc5ac333-7088-55b5-8dff-47ad3124a244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287574 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287574 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287574 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287574 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186285503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287574 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cfb29df0-619b-574f-9a2b-69bb58650179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186287018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186287068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186286495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287666 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffd48eaf-9d9e-5aaf-ad75-c7d452ae0613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186466700 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186466701 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186466702 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A=\\{{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\}$\n\n- **II.** $B=\\{{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\}$\n\n- **III.** $C=\\{{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "614d2565-08b2-5cdc-9df9-02ccb7032ebd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287712 #edb/ref 1074 "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,…\\}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $B$ contains four elements:\n\n$$\nB=\\{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=4,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=2{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,2{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,…\\}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set $\\{2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}\\}$ given below.\n\n$\\{2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}\\}=\\{z\\in C\\,:\\,{z}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n${z}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1cb23c2-1fc6-50c0-a109-f29b4b4fe8eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287732 #edb/ref 1074 "The given set contains the roots $z\\in C$ of some cubic polynomial $p(z).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=2,$ ${z}_{2}=3-\\text{i},$ and ${z}_{3}=3+\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2})(z-{z}_{3}) \\\\  & =(1)(z-2)(z-(3-\\text{i}))(z-(3+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(z-2)({z}^{2}-z(3+\\text{i})-z(3-\\text{i})+(3-\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(z-2)({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & ={z}^{3}-6{z}^{2}+10z-2{z}^{2}+12z-20 \\\\  & ={z}^{3}-8{z}^{2}+22z-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n\\{2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}\\}=\\{z\\in C\\,:\\,{z}^{3}-8{z}^{2}+22z-20=0\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
